BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Tech Lancaster
UID:event_313614672@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260420T032738Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T203000
SUMMARY:Tech Lancaster Meetup
DESCRIPTION:Tech Lancaster Meetups\nWe will be upstairs in "The Sanctuary"
  - when you walk in the main entrance just head up the stairs! We will hav
 e signs as you walk in to guide you.\nPizza is provided free upstairs. Bee
 r/wine/soda/etc at the bar downstairs!\n\nThis months speakers:\n**Luke We
 stfall - *Actually… it IS rocket science ***\nAt some point\, every Kerb
 al engineer gets tired of manually throttling up and watching their rocket
  cartwheel into the ocean. In this talk\, we'll use Kerbal Space Program\,
  a beloved space flight simulator where failure is half the fun\, as a pla
 yground for exploring two approaches to automation: the onboard scripting 
 of kOS and the external control API of kRPC. Along the way\, we'll discove
 r what they can teach us about flight dynamics\, control loops\, and why s
 ometimes the best debugging session involves a tiny green astronaut.\n\n**
 Ken Richards - *Walk Up Song ***\nCome see if Ken’s app can guess your a
 ge and pick a song you’ll vibe to. Then stick around — he’ll share t
 he creative story\, lessons on large vs. small models\, and where AI can f
 all short.\n\nTypical schedule of events:\n\n6:30 PM Doors Open/Pizza/Ming
 le\n\n7:00 PM Introduction/Announcements\n\n7:05 PM First Speaker\n\n7:35 
 PM Break\n\n7:45 PM Speaker 2\n\n8:15 PM End
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/tech-lancaster-meetups/events/3136146
 72/
